.SH "NAME"
roark\-calendar\-connection\-list \- List calendar connections
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark calendar\-connection list
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Returns every calendar connection in the authenticated project, by label. A project has a handful of these, so the list is not paginated: `pagination.hasMore` is always false.
.SH "API"
GET /v1/calendar\-connection
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-provider\fR \fI<value>\fR
Who holds the calendar. CAL_COM is the only provider that can be connected today; GOOGLE and CALENDLY are described by `capabilities` but not yet connectable. One of: CAL_COM, GOOGLE, CALENDLY. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
